<46-x-2>{\selectlanguage {english}\color {blue}\bfseries \LRnum {X4.105}~}{\bfseries \selectlanguage {iast}}\ekdsep {\selectlanguage {english}\xexclude {\getsiglum {Gr2,Gr3} have a different verse order: 4.50cd (except \getsiglum {E2}) \textrightarrow \ 4.51 \textrightarrow \ \ref {anahata} \textrightarrow \ 4.50. }\getsiglum {Gr2,V19} have 4.50cd\,=\,X4.105cd twice. The first time (a), their reading of the last pāda is closer to the \textalpha \ reading \textit {avadhāryāpi yoginaḥ}, while the second time (b) it is \textit {avagamyā hi yogibhiḥ}, which is closer to the reading of the expanded version.}</46-x-2>
